{"type":"thinking","text":"At 0x066F=32, 0x0670=0: all three tiles are 102 (empty/peach) → 0 filled hearts! So the display shows 0 hearts (3 empty containers).\n\nWait, that means the player would be dead. But the game didn't die (we wrote the value; death is triggered by damage events). So the display shows 0 filled hearts.\n\nSo mapping:\n- 0x066F=34, 0x0670=0xFF → 3 full hearts\n- 0x066F=33, 0x0670=0xFF? (I set 0x0670=0xFF earlier at 34; when I wrote 33 I didn't change 0x0670) → 2 full + 1 empty\n- 0x066F=32, 0x0670=0 → 3 empty (0 full)\n- 0x066F=31, 0x0670=0 → 2 tiles full (242,242)? That was transient.\n\nHmm, 33→2 full, 34→3 full, 32→0 full. Non-monotonic: 33→2, 32→0, 34→3.\n\nHmm! Maybe the display isn't a simple function of 0x066F but uses BOTH 0x066F and 0x0670. Let me reconsider:\n- 34 (0x22) + 0xFF → 3 full\n- 33 (0x21) + 0xFF → 2 full + 1 empty\n- 32 (0x20) + 0x00 → 0 full\n- 31 (0x1F) + 0x00 → ? (transient 2 full)\n\nHypothesis: health (half-hearts) = 0x066F & 0x0F? no. Let me think: maybe health = 0x066F - 0x20 + (0x0670 >= 0x80 ? 0 : ...)? \n\nAlternatively, maybe 0x066F is not health; maybe 0x0670 is health (0xFF → 3 hearts, 0x00 → 0 hearts), and 0x066F+0x0670 together form a 16-bit value.\n\nWait! Let's consider 0x066F and 0x0670 as a 16-bit little-endian value H = 0x0670*256 + 0x066F:\n- Full: 0xFF22 = 65314\n- 33,0xFF: 0xFF21 = 65313\n- 32,0x00: 0x0020 = 32\n- 31,0x00: 0x001F = 31\n\nHmm, full = 65314 and 33 = 65313 (differ by 1). And 32,0 = 32. So the full-range value decreasing by 1 per hit, then wrapping to 32 when 0x0670=0? Weird.\n\nAlternatively big-endian: H = 0x066F*256 + 0x0670:\n- 34,255: 0x22FF = 8959\n- 33,255: 0x21FF = 8703\n- 32,0: 0x2000 = 8192\n\nHmm.\n\nMaybe the actual health variable is elsewhere and these two bytes are related but not the display source. But 0x0670=0 → 0 hearts strongly suggests 0x0670 is health (0 = dead/none, 0xFF = full).\n\nLet me test: set 0x066F=34 (full) but 0x0670=0x00 → if display shows 0 hearts, then 0x0670 is the display source. And set 0x066F=32, 0x0670=0xFF → if 3 hearts, confirm.\n\nGiven the last test: 0x066F=32, 0x0670=0 → 0 hearts. And 0x066F=34,0x0670=0xFF → 3 hearts. So 0x0670 could be the source.\n\nEarlier: 0x066F=31, 0x0670=0 → 2 full hearts?! That contradicts 0x0670=0→0 hearts. Unless transient.\n\nLet me do clean tests with pause+step:\nTest A: 0x066F=34, 0x0670=0x00 → ?\nTest B: 0x066F=32, 0x0670=0xFF → ?\nTest C: 0x066F=31, 0x0670=0x00 → ? (redo cleanly)\n\nLet me do Test A: write 0x066F=34, 0x0670=0. Then step 60. Read nametable.\n\nActually wait, the game might re-derive 0x066F from 0x0670 or vice versa during the step (e.g., the death check). But no damage so probably not.\n\nLet me run tests. Test A."}
