ral 1-hit display. If the game shows half hearts, then health has half-heart granularity. Full = 6 half. The natural hit sequence (from the watch) 0x066F 34→33→32 with 0x0670 cycling. If each hit removes 1 half-heart, then after 1 hit health=5 half, 2 hits=4, 3=3, 4=2, 5=1, 6=0 (death). But 0x066F only went 34→33→32 before death, i.e., 3 values for 6 hits? That means 0x066F changes every 2 hits (1 full heart). So 0x066F = full hearts roughly, and 0x0670 = the half flag. That fits: 0x066F = 0x20 + full_hearts? full 3→0x23? but it's 0x22. Hmm, 0x20 + (hearts-1): full 3→0x22 ✓, 2 hearts→0x21 ✓, 1 heart→0x20 ✓, 0 hearts→0x1F. But at death we read 0x20 (not 0x1F). Maybe the death routine sets 0x20.\n\nHmm, so at death the display showed 0 hearts but 0x066F=0x20. If 0x066F=0x20 means 1 heart, the display contradicts. Unless the display uses 0x0670=0 to force 0 hearts.\n\nFormula: full_hearts_shown = (0x066F - 0x20) + (0x0670 >= 0x80 ? 1 : 0)? At death (32,0): 0+0=0 ✓. At (33,127): 1+0=1 full + half → 1.5 ✓. At (34,255): 2+1=3 ✓. At (33,255): 1+1=2 ✓. At (34,0): 2+0=2 ✓.\nAnd half = (0x0670 > 0 && 0x0670 < 0x80).\n\nSo the display: full hearts = (H-0x20) + (F>=0x80), half = (F>0 && F<0x80).\n\nHmm OK. Actually maybe simpler: the game likely has a health variable = 2*(H-0x20) + (F>=0x80 ? 1 : 0) in half-hearts, but when F==0 (dead) it's... 2*(H-0x20). At death 32,0 → 0 half. Consistent! And the display shows floor(health_half/2) full + (health_half odd ? half) + empties.\n\nLet's test: health_half = 2*(H-0x20) + (F>=0x80 ? 1 : 0):\n- (34,255): 2*2+1=5 → display 2 full + 1 half? But observed 3 full (242,242,242). ✗.\n\nHmm. So not.\n\nOK I'll just go with the empirical rule and describe it as \"how many hearts are filled\". Honestly, for the user's purposes, the address is the key deliverable.\n\nHmm, wait. Actually, let me reconsider the possibility that the real health variable is 0x066F alone with the encoding: full_hearts = 0x066F - 0x1F, and 0x0670 is a SEPARATE \"damage flash\" variable, and the (34,0)→2 result is an artifact of the game's incremental redraw (it didn't fully update when I wrote 0x0670=0). Let me test (34,0) with a FRESH redraw via the pause screen — I did that: pause screen showed 242,242,102 (2 full). So even a fresh redraw gives 2. So 0x0670 does affect the display.\n\nHmm, unless the pause screen doesn't fully redraw hearts.\n\nUgh. Let me try yet another decisive test: set (34,255) and confirm 3 full via pause screen; set (32,127) — predict from my rule: (32,127): full = 0 + 0 = 0 full + half → 0.5 hearts. Let me test and see if a half heart appears. This distinguishes.\n\nActually, my rule predicts (32,127) → 0 full + 1 half = 0.5. Let me test. And (32,255) → 1 full (242,102,102).\n\nLet me test (32,255): predict 242,102,102 (1 full).\nAnd (32,127): predict 101,102,102 (1 half).\n\nLet me run both. Currently inventory open with (33,127) showing 242,101,102.\n\nTest A: write 0x066F=32, 0x0670=255, close+open inventory, read. Predict 242,102,102.\nTest B: write 0x066F=32, 0x0670=127, close+open, read. Predict 101,102,102.\n\nHmm, but the \"close+open\" to redraw requires the game to run; the game might change values. Let me keep it simple.\n\nActually, the value persists (we read back). Let me do test A.\n\nCurrently inventory open. Sequence: play_input start (close), write 32,255, play_input start (open), read.\n\nLet me do A."}
