irst char is the icon (rupee/key/bomb) and the second is the digit. Wait, the screenshot showed a rupee icon then \"X0\". Hmm, maybe the icon is the sprite-like graphic and \"X0\" is... Actually let me look: the HUD row has tiles 105,11,107 at cols 15,16,17 and 105,10,107 at 18,19,20. Hmm, so two groups of 3 tiles each per counter row? That's odd.\n\nWhatever — writing a distinctive value like 5 should change the display visibly. Let me just try candidates and screenshot.\n\nLet me test 0x066D=5: write, press start (if inventory open, close first), open inventory, screenshot.\n\nCurrently the game is running (inventory closed, on enemy screen). Let me write 0x066D=5, 0x066E=0, then press start, screenshot.\n\nActually, writing while on the enemy screen risks a hit, but fine.\n\nLet me do: write 0x066D=5, 0x066E=0; play_input start 20; screenshot.\n\nThen examine the rupee counter.\n\nLet me go."}
