ttom is: rupees, keys, bombs. So row2=keys, row3=bombs. And 0x066D=rupees, 0x066E=keys. Good. Now bombs = the byte controlling row3.\n\nLet me test 0x067C. Currently 0x067C=8. Write 0x067C=5 and redraw; if row3 changes to 5, 0x067C is the bomb count (or max bombs). But actually the bomb count starts at 0 and max bombs = 8. If 0x067C=8 is max bombs, writing 5 would change... it would display 5 if the row shows current bombs? Hmm. The row currently shows 0 (current bombs). If I write 0x067C=5 and row3 shows 5, then 0x067C is the displayed bomb count (but it was 8 before, showing 0 — contradiction). So 0x067C=8 is NOT the displayed count (since display shows 0 while 0x067C=8). So the bomb count is another byte (0), and 0x067C is max bombs.\n\nSo the bomb count is 0 and I need to find which byte it is. Candidates: 0x067B, 0x067D, 0x067E, 0x067F (all 0). Let me test each by writing 5 and checking row3.\n\nLet me test 0x067D=5 first (common: bombs at 0x067C, max at 0x067D? or vice versa).\n\nHmm, we know 0x067C=8. In Zelda, max bombs = 8 at start. So 0x067C = max bombs. Then current bombs = 0x067D? Let me test.\n\nLet me write 0x067D=5, redraw, screenshot.\n\nI'm in the inventory. Close, write, open.\n\nActually, I can write multiple candidates at once? If I write 5 to 0x067B,0x067D,0x067E,0x067F all at once and row3 shows 5, then one of them is it, but I won't know which. Let me do one at a time. Start with 0x067D.\n\nLet me do close, write 0x067D=5, open, screenshot.\n\nHmm, each cycle is 3 calls. Let me instead write to 5 candidates sequentially? No.\n\nAlternatively, I can write a distinctive value to each and read the display. Let me just test 0x067B=5 (many games store current then max).\n\nActually, let me reason: the known Zelda map: $067C = Bombs, $067D = MaxBombs, $067E = Keys? Hmm. But we found keys at 0x066E. Hmm, that's weird.\n\nWait, maybe I mis-assigned rows. What if row2 (0x066E) is actually the BOMB count and row3 is keys? Let me verify the icons rigorously.\n\nLet me read the tiles at the icon positions on the pause screen. In the pause screen, the counters are at nametable rows 6-8 and cols ~10-16. Let me read nametable x=8 y=6 width=16 height=3.\n\nActually, easier: let me use the game screen (not pause) where the HUD is at rows 3-5 cols 10-20. We read row 3: cols 12=33,13=0,15-20=105,11,107,105,10,107. Row 4: 15,17,18,20=108. Row 5: 12=33,13=0,15-20=108,36,108,108,36,108.\n\nHmm, so the counters are at cols 15-20 in rows 3,4,5, each row a counter with two 3-tile groups? Actually cols 15-17 and 18-20, each 3 tiles. Hmm, maybe each counter displays 2 digits, each digit being ~1.5 tiles? No.\n\nHmm, actually maybe the layout is: cols 15-17 = icon + digit? Let me read the tiles 105,11,107,108,10,36.\n\nThis is a rabbit hole. Let me just visually confirm the icons by cropping? I can't crop. But I can get_tile_at_pixel at the icon location and read the tile. On the game screen, the rupee row is row 3 col 12-13 (tiles 33 and 0?). Hmm.\n\nLet me just trust the standard Zelda HUD order: rupee, key, bomb. So row2=keys (0x066E), row3=bombs.\n\nNow find the bomb count. Test 0x067D.\n\nLet me do it.\n\nActually, to be efficient, let me write a DIFFERENT value to each candidate in one pass and observe which row changes... no, they all would.\n\nOK one at a time. 0x067D first.\n\nHmm, wait — actually maybe the bomb count is 0x066F? No, that's hearts.\n\nLet me think about where the game would store bombs. The hearts are at 0x0650/0x066F. The counters are at 0x066D (rupees) and 0x066E (keys). Bombs likely at a nearby byte. Candidates: 0x066C, 0x066B, 0x066A, 0x0671..0x067F. We read 0x0660-0x066E all zero except hearts; 0x066D/0x066E now. 0x066A-0x066C = 0. 0x0671-0x067B = 0. 0x067C=8.\n\nLet me test 0x067C first (maybe it IS the bomb count and max bombs is elsewhere; but display showed 0 while 0x067C=8, so no).\n\nTest 0x067D=5.\n\nLet me do it."}
